  "drawnOn": "A388",
  "description": "The 2023 scheme with the UAE flag carried from the tail along the rear half of the fuselage, as a waving ribbon: a red block (the flag's hoist) standing from the crown to the wing root just aft of 'Emirates', then green along the crown from it, the white between, and black sweeping down from the fin's root across the rear fuselage to low on the side behind the wing; the tail's red sweep, flag ribbon fin, gold titles, red belly panel, gold engine logo and red winglets are the standard's. No Arabic title (the red block stands where it was).",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.emirates.com/media-centre/emirates-unveils-a-striking-new-uae-flag-livery-on-its-a380/",
      "title": "Emirates unveils a striking new UAE flag livery on its A380 (press release, 8 May 2026)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-22",
      "note": "A6-EVG; the UAE's colours in a 3D design across both sides, extending the tail's design; part of the 'This Flag Will Always Fly' campaign; already flown to New York and Brisbane; a similar design planned for one 777. Read through its reprints (World Airline News, Gulf News)."
    },
