  "notes": "Drawn on the A380 (A6-EVG), from the two 2026 Commons photos, one each side; the two sides carry the same layout. The flag's bands are drawn as their big masses; on the aircraft they're shaded in 3D, with the white and black in fine ripple lines like the fin's, and the white between the green and the black is left as the base white. Below the wing root the red block isn't seen in either photo (the wing, fairing and engines hide it): drawn ending at the fairing, and how far it runs toward the belly isn't known. The black's rounded lower end is seen only from below at an angle (left photo); white runs under it to the belly's red title panel, the 2023 scheme's, seen in the left photo between the engines. On the right the black's front is hidden under the wing, so its front edge is the left photo's. The fin, winglets, engines and titles are the 2023 scheme's (UAE/standard and its A380 titles), checked on both photos; the Arabic title isn't painted (the red block is where it would be). The press release says a similar flag is planned for one 777: not seen in an open photo yet (A6-EQH is a lead, in TODO).",
  "history": "A6-EVG was repainted in the 2023 scheme by early 2025 (Commons, 2025-02 and 2025-06); the flag was added and unveiled on 8 May 2026."
}
